home-library (5.4.0+git20261003.48582bb-1~ppa4~ubuntu26.04.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * home-library-failover: do not stop the units when the package is
    upgraded. With --no-start alone, debhelper stopped them in preinst and
    never started them again, and stopping home-library-db on the active
    node runs db-release: upgrading racknerd to ~ppa3 handed the library to
    homelab. Pass --no-stop-on-upgrade.
  * home-library-failover: README.Debian says that removing the package
    from the active node hands the library over, and how to avoid that.

 -- Robert August Vincent II (Bob) <pillarsdotnet@gmail.com>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 14:06:23 -0400

home-library (5.4.0+git20261003.48582bb-1~ppa3~ubuntu26.04.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * home-library-failover: point public DNS at the active node. When
    DDNS_HOSTNAME is set, vip-claim updates that name through Hurricane
    Electric's dynamic DNS once the app is healthy, from the node's own
    public address, so a handoff moves the public site as well as the VIP.
    Failures are logged and never stop the node serving.
  * home-library-failover: `enable` also starts the hourly sync timer,
    instead of leaving it for the next boot.

 -- Robert August Vincent II (Bob) <pillarsdotnet@gmail.com>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 13:09:11 -0400

home-library (5.4.0+git20261003.48582bb-1~ppa2~ubuntu26.04.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * New binary package home-library-failover: hands the library between two
    nodes with the native package, replacing the container-era scripts in
    deploy/. It keeps their ownership generations and refusal to promote
    on a guess, and adds:
    - checkpoints and snapshots with sqlite3 as the home-library user,
      instead of inside the container image;
    - health checks through the app's Unix socket;
    - drop-ins that gate home-library.socket as well as the service on the
      activity flag, so a request cannot start the app on a standby;
    - a manual to-local that works on the non-preferred node, and with
      FORCE=1 when the owner is unreachable;
    - the hourly disaster copy as a systemd timer instead of cron.
    Installing it changes nothing until `home-library-failover enable`.

 -- Robert August Vincent II (Bob) <pillarsdotnet@gmail.com>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 01:47:55 -0400

